  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "With **IMPERIAL KNIGHTS** as your Army Faction, you must set your army's Oath once Read Mission Objectives is over. An Oath is 1 Deed and 1 Quality; for each, pick an entry or roll a D6 on its table.\n\nDeeds:\n\n- We vow to lay low the tyrant... (1–2): as the battle begins, choose 1 enemy **CHARACTER** model; the Deed is achieved as any turn ends once that model is **destroyed**.\n- We swear to reclaim the realm... (3–4): the Deed is achieved as your opponent's turn ends if they control fewer objective markers than you.\n- We pledge to reap a great tally... (5–6): the Deed is achieved as a battle round ends if the enemy units destroyed in that round outnumber its number (e.g. 2 in round 1), even ones later returned to the battlefield.\n\nQualities, which apply for the rest of the battle to every model of yours that has this ability:\n\n- ...with all our martial valour risen over all. (1–2): whenever the model is picked to shoot or fight, 1 **Hit roll** and 1 **Wound roll** can be re-rolled.\n- ...and we are eager for the challenge. (3–4): it gets +2\" Move, and +1 to its Advance and **Charge rolls**.\n- ...yet shall our legacy be unsullied. (5–6): it gets +2 Objective Control and +1 Leadership.\n\nThe first time your Deed is achieved, the Oath is fulfilled: your army is Honoured for the rest of the battle, and you get 2CP, or 3CP if either part was rolled. These CP are exempt from the Core Rules cap of 1CP gained per battle round.",
